course: dictionary
lesson: 5522
title: Least and at least
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Least» means the smallest amount. The one with the least has less than all the others.
explain: «At least» means that number or more, never fewer. «At least 3 coins» means 3 coins or more.
explain: «At least» can also mean «anyway, there is one good thing». «It rained, but at least we had umbrellas.» The rain was bad, but the umbrellas were a good thing.
fact: «Least» means the smallest amount.
fact: «At least» means that number or more, not fewer.
fact: «Not in the least» means not at all.
fact: «The least I can do» means the smallest thing you should do, such as «at least say thank you».
fact: «Least» can be an adjective, an adverb or a pronoun, and it belongs to the same family as little and less.
exercise: «Children should be active for at least an hour a day.» What does at least mean here? | Only in the morning | Less than an hour | Exactly one hour and no more | *An hour or more
exercise: «It rained, but at least we had umbrellas.» What is the one good thing? | *We had umbrellas | The umbrellas were broken | The rain stopped early | It did not rain at all
exercise: Which phrase means «not at all»? | *Not in the least | Last but not least | The least I can do | At least
test: «A satnav finds its position by timing radio signals from at least four satellites.» What does at least four mean? | Exactly three satellites | *Four or more satellites | Only one satellite | Fewer than four satellites
test: In «14 + 12 - 5 = 21», the word «least» in «at least one» means what? | *One or more | Exactly zero | A number that is less than one | The smallest of all the numbers in the sum
exam: Which sentence uses «least» to mean the smallest amount? | It is at least a good day, so we are happy | She said thank you at least once | I did not mind in the least | *The team with the least points lost the game
